WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.706
You own a bike worth three hundred dollars and a phone worth two hundred. You owe your sister one hundred. What is really yours? Five hundred minus one hundred: four hundred dollars.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:35.028
A business is the same. What it owns are assets. What it owes are liabilities. The difference is equity, the owner's capital. When a trader keeps no full records, we list the assets and liabilities at a date. That list is a statement of affairs.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:47.071
First, sort each balance into assets or liabilities. Careful: a bank overdraft is money owed to the bank, so it is a liability.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:52.984
Next, use the carrying amount for non-current assets: cost minus the depreciation so far.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:01:01.057
Then add up total assets and total liabilities separately, and take one from the other. That is equity.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:14.364
To find profit, compare closing equity with opening equity. Add back drawings, because they took equity out. Take off new capital, because it was put in, not earned.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:28.423
Here is a real question from November 2023. Ed is a sole trader. Calculate his equity at the first of May 2022. Three marks.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:37.850
Here are Ed's balances. Fixtures and fittings cost one hundred and twenty-three thousand five hundred, with depreciation of fifty-five thousand five hundred and seventy-five.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:45.716
The carrying amount is one hundred and twenty-three thousand five hundred minus fifty-five thousand five hundred and seventy-five: sixty-seven thousand nine hundred and twenty-five.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:54.914
Add the assets: fixtures, bank, inventory and trade receivables. Total assets are one hundred and seventy-one thousand, one hundred and five dollars.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:03.023
Liabilities are other payables, one thousand four hundred, and trade payables, twenty-five thousand one hundred: twenty-six thousand five hundred in total.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:15.226
Equity is one hundred and seventy-one thousand, one hundred and five, minus twenty-six thousand five hundred: one hundred and forty-four thousand, six hundred and five dollars. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:23.457
A common mistake is adding non-current assets at cost. Use the carrying amount.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:31.938
Another is forgetting drawings when finding profit. Drawings lowered closing equity, so add them back.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:42.194
Now you try. Find Nadia's equity at the end of the year, then her profit. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:58.689
Equipment is twelve thousand minus three thousand: nine thousand. Assets total nineteen thousand seven hundred. The overdraft and payables make four thousand seven hundred. Equity is fifteen thousand dollars.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:10.720
Equity fell by three thousand. Add back drawings of nine thousand: six thousand. Take off the new capital of two thousand. Profit is four thousand dollars.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:22.660
Remember: assets minus liabilities gives equity. The change in equity, plus drawings, minus new capital, gives profit. Now try the practice questions.
